SUMMARY:Hawaiian History Talk Story-Paniolo History
DESCRIPTION:In the earliest days of the Kingdom\, cattle and then horses 
 arrived on ships from faraway lands. The cattle multiplied so quickly th
 at the Hawaiian people asked for relief from the King\, and Spanish spea
 king Vaqueros were contracted to come to the islands and control the her
 ds. They taught the cowboy arts to any kanaka willing to learn\, leaving
  an indelible mark on the islands for all time.…  https://www.librarie
 shawaii.org/event/hawaiian-history-talk-story/  Sources: Libraries https
 ://www.librarieshawaii.org/event/hawaiian-history-talk-story/
LOCATION:North Kohala Public Library (Hawai‘i)
URL:https://www.librarieshawaii.org/event/hawaiian-history-talk-story/
CATEGORIES:Library programs
END:VEVENT
